      "title": "Home values fall for seventh consecutive month as interest rates dent demand",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/02/home-values-fall-for-seventh-month-interest-rates-dent-property-demand",
      "description": "<p>Centre of downturn shifts away from Sydney and Melbourne, but after such strong growth most homeowners still sit on sizeable gains</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australian home values have dropped for a seventh consecutive month, with prices in the capital cities now falling at the fastest pace in 40 years as rising mortgage rates scare off buyers.</p><p>Cotality data shows the centre of the downturn is also shifting away from Sydney and Melbourne toward the mid-sized state capital cities, with Brisbane and Perth leading October’s declines.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/02/home-values-fall-for-seventh-month-interest-rates-dent-property-demand\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-01T14:00:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "Former NSW Liberal leads overhaul of One Nation candidate selection process",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/02/former-nsw-liberal-leads-overhaul-of-one-nation-candidate-selection-process-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive:</strong> Mark Jones, once on track for one of the Liberal party’s most powerful roles, is now instrumental in One Nation’s expansion</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>In 2023, a young and ambitious Liberal moderate was on the brink of securing one of the most powerful roles in the party: state director of the New South Wales branch. Three years later, he is playing a key role in selecting and vetting One Nation candidates determined to beat his former colleagues.</p><p>Multiple Liberal sources familiar with recruitment for the position, which involves running election campaigns and managing fundraising, confirm Mark Jones was among the final three candidates for the role before his career advancement was ultimately blocked.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/02/former-nsw-liberal-leads-overhaul-of-one-nation-candidate-selection-process-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-01T14:00:15"
    },
