      "title": "Northern Territory water plan condemned as ‘blatant and shameless’ attack on nature",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/02/northern-territory-water-plan-condemned-as-blatant-and-shameless-attack-on-nature",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive</strong>: Move to scrap legal requirement to set aside water for environment is ‘extreme even for the NT CLP government’, green group says</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Northern Territory government has been accused of making a “blatant and shameless” attack on nature by planning to delete a legal requirement that water must be allocated to the environment.</p><p>In what has been described as the latest in a series of attacks on the environment by the NT’s Country Liberal party, the Finocchiaro government plans to change water rules that govern how much ground and surface water industry can take.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/02/northern-territory-water-plan-condemned-as-blatant-and-shameless-attack-on-nature\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-01T14:00:13"
    },
